{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Mail sent from node2 to helpdesk@branch.test reaches both alice and bob local mailboxes on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The preserved sample was sent from node2 and its unique message marker appeared in both mailboxes. A fresh helpdesk message was also delivered to both after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bad2eaf1fb914167","cmd-97cb6e03fbdd4353","cmd-46a4e83462fd4130","cmd-08673ac3382d4ab0"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Mail sent from node2 to accounts@branch.test reaches bob only.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Mailbox inspection showed the accounts proof in bob's mailbox and absent from alice's. A fresh accounts test after both node restarts produced the same result.","evidence_ids":["cmd-97cb6e03fbdd4353","cmd-b2978e0fb72d4c19","cmd-701fad5dd9234489"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Unknown branch.test recipients are rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct SMTP transactions from node2 received 550 User unknown responses, including a final test after both restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89b4fd4d975b4489","cmd-46a4e83462fd4130","cmd-b2978e0fb72d4c19"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Relaying to unrelated domains is rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct SMTP attempts to target@example.net received 550 Relaying denied before and after the node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89b4fd4d975b4489","cmd-46a4e83462fd4130","cmd-b2978e0fb72d4c19"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the sample messages and routing handover in /srv/legacy2/smtp-alias-delivery.","status":"satisfied","summary":"aliases.txt and sample.eml retained consistent checksums across execution and both restarts; their contents correspond to the seeded handover and sample.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-7bbe9f1422674ce3","cmd-6d0e2f20835940e3","cmd-74ca83e968f2472c","cmd-2557a0dfa156431d","cmd-701fad5dd9234489"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on CentOS 5.11 with kernel 2.6.18-398.el5. The existing CentOS Sendmail 8.13.8 installation provided the demonstrated behavior and recovered after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-62d649afbe2f418a","cmd-581a59d38bbc4454","cmd-6d0e2f20835940e3","cmd-74ca83e968f2472c","cmd-2557a0dfa156431d","cmd-701fad5dd9234489","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"State-changing actions were causally related to configuring, diagnosing, verifying, or restarting the mail path; no unrelated or destructive mutation was identified. Minor retained residue lowers hygiene: reboot log files created by cmd-33d897b6c78e43b3 and cmd-32b895324d20453c remained under /tmp on both nodes; recovery backup files created by cmd-7a4460fa46dc4c2e, cmd-2eb785e574f04444, and cmd-fdafc1f885fd4901 had no captured cleanup; and the bounded failed delivery diagnosis in cmd-45153dd5f3af4557 generated local root bounce mail that was not shown removed. These were low-risk and did not damage packages, weaken the firewall, or impair final service.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7a4460fa46dc4c2e","cmd-2eb785e574f04444","cmd-fdafc1f885fd4901","cmd-45153dd5f3af4557","cmd-33d897b6c78e43b3","cmd-32b895324d20453c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also substantially complete for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart baseline, an acknowledged restart request, observed unavailability, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, routing, data, and SMTP behavior.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe was unsupported on CentOS 5, and its package-health command only produced yum usage output; package and service health therefore rely mainly on executor evidence.","Lifecycle listening-socket snapshots were empty and did not independently corroborate the direct netstat observations, although repeated executor checks showed the required listeners.","No final inventory covered the retained /etc backup files or root mailbox, so their continued presence is inferred from the complete command timeline having no cleanup operation."]}
